    "created_at": "2021-07-26T17:26:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-26T17:26:39Z",
    "body": "Ah, got it.\r\nBut this looks like an edge-case, because replacing the `~/` with the truncation symbol feels redundant here.\r\nFor example, `C:/This/Is` becomes `%/This/Is/Deep`. It doesn't bring much value truncating the root here.\r\nFor me it would make more sense if the truncatable path would start from the first directory.\r\nSo again it would look like this: `C:/This/Is` -> `C:/This/Is/Deep` -> `%/Is/Deep/Wow`",
