    "created_at": "2021-07-26T17:50:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-26T17:50:51Z",
    "body": "If I set it to 4 the misunderstanding won't go anywhere. I'll just be getting the confusing truncation one level deeper.\r\n`~/a/b` -> `~/a/b/c` -> `%/a/b/c/d`\r\n\r\nMy point here is that the root sign usually is too short to make it part of the truncatable set.\r\nThe current logic would make more sense if the root was represented by a some kind of a long uuid string, but it's only 2 chars and it's not dynamic like a directory name. It's always 2 chars.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I got you and I think you got me. I agree that it's not a bug, but could be a feature request to make the root level optional for truncation.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
